Z||000000||Seanh||02-10-2001||02:02 AM||||Some one is signing me up for tons of crap on the net. I get about 10 emails a day due to this person. I have no idea who it is. They are going around to internet sites and signing my email address up for all kinds of usless information. How can I find out who is doing it? Is there any way since he is not sending me the email directly. Would one of the internet sites be able to help me out with his IP address maybe? Anyone know anything about how to deal with this problem? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto (3.4 Conversion in Progress)<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||02-10-2001||02:33 AM||||I think we all have this problem. My hotmail account gets about 60 sex and how to make money fast  emails a day. I don't even use it anymore. Some email companies sell your address, especially the free ones. Some companies, any of them you gave your email address to- sell your address too. It's big business, and it only takes one to sell it. Time to change your address-- should be free.<P>&gt;&gt;Got any good sub ideas for the fiero?  I'm thinking of trying fierosound's firewall sub. What do you think?&lt;&lt;<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- project &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||02-10-2001||07:25 PM||||This was happening to me also for a while.  The way I found out which companies were doing it was this.  I would use a fake name when I signed up for things that required a name.  Just like sign up sites and such, nothing where I pay for things obviously.  Anyway, I would use Bill for yahoo or Sam for another site, or what have you.  I copied down what name I used in a word file.  Then, when I would get those emails, if you look in them, often times you will find one of the fake names you used.  Go back to the word document and look it up, then contact or call the company and give them hell.  Or report them to that spam site, forget what it is.  It usually works too, but I still get the occasional one, recently its been "Debt Consolidation".  Have to figure it out...||||reg||12
Z||000003||Seanh||02-10-2001||08:45 PM||||I will have to do that. I am thinking it is someone locally, probally at school who really hates me. The reason I think this is becuase one site in particular, that I get their newsletter in the email. There was a link at the bottem of the page about changing your account information. So I clicked it, website asked for my email and password to log into my account (I know for a fact I never signed up for this). I click "forgot password" and it gave me "my hint" which was "my name", so I tired "sean" and it said it had to be atleast 6 letters long. I click "Email my password to me" and I got the email saying my pass was "SOMESEAN" I know I never signed up for this, and I am sure some one who knows me is the one signing my up for all this crap. I am really getting ticked off. I report it all to Spamcop.net if thats what your thinking of. I might subscribe to their email services and use them as my email provider. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||02-11-2001||12:49 AM||||I saw somewhere when a web site has an https beginning, it's safe and secure.  When I see one that isn't and asks for my name, I also make some up.  Try to be creative.  One time I got pissed off and put my street name as:  mindyourownf*c*ngbusinessyoustupidpiecesofsh*t avenue.  Try getting that one through the post office.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hank is Here||02-11-2001||01:15 AM||||Well i must admit I am a criminal at this.  My sophmore year I signed up my accounting teacher at fat_accountant@beer.com or something like that.  It was all in good fun with him.  I let all the meaasages drain into his other account at the university for like two weeks or so.  About two weeks later I gave him all his passwords.  He was the only teacher that I stayed after class and traided drinknig stories with and beat me, I still resent that.  This is not hard to do, at least I tried to do it with taste.<BR>||||reg||1
